WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:02.370
- [Nurse] Here we go.

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.990
- I definitely think
that it's gonna become

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:07.050
one of those things that
just happens at universities

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:09.750
of submitting your vaccination record.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:10.610
- I know of a lot of people

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.920
who've stayed home for
first and second semester,

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.060
but I think a lot of them

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:16.530
are planning to come
to campus in the fall.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.950
- [Narrator] A growing number
of colleges around the country

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:20.900
will require students get vaccinated

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.480
before returning to campus in the fall.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.490
- That means a lot more in-person events,

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:28.823
in person activities and classes.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.070
Of course masks and social distancing

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:34.410
may still be a part of campus life,

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:37.070
but certainly more
classes will be happening

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.640
inside the class than they have this year.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.740
- [Narrator] But the mandates
are stirring up controversy

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.880
about the legality, and whether colleges

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:46.940
can make vaccinations a
condition of attendance.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:48.350
Will the requirements help campus

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:51.020
return to some semblance
of normal in the fall?

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:53.390
Or will there be legal setbacks?

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:56.380
(light upbeat music)

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:59.450
For Northeastern, a private
university in Boston,

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.840
the school says herd
immunity is the best path

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.330
to return its 18,000 undergraduates

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.520
to fully in-person classes.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.620
- The magic of an undergraduate degree

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:10.430
is that you're close to your friends

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:13.370
and you're close to your
classmates and you learn together.

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:16.470
But that same thing that makes
it so rich and interesting

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:18.730
does allow the virus to spread.

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:21.160
- [Narrator] Northeastern
Administrator, Michael Armini,

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:23.440
believes the school is
on solid legal ground

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:24.870
with the requirements.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:28.010
- So we're gonna require
the COVID-19 vaccine

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:28.860
for the same reason

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.560
that we have always required
vaccinations of students,

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:35.010
whether it's for measles
or mumps or meningitis,

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:36.810
and it's to keep the community safe.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:40.330
- [Narrator] Northeastern
reopened last fall,

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:41.930
but with frequent COVID testing,

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:45.770
social distancing protocols,
and limited in-person classes.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:48.240
- You never know if
someone has coronavirus.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:52.640
So it's just that whole issue
of I want to meet new people.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.820
I want to get into my
new college environment.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:56.680
But is it safe to do so yet?

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.340
I'd say that was the biggest stressor

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.440
of going to college this year,

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:02.393
which was definitely unique for our class.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.560
- [Narrator] Cole
Clericuzio is a freshmen,

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.550
and says his experience has
been anything but normal.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.800
He works part time as an EMT,

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.860
treating COVID patients up close.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:16.100
So he jumped at the
opportunity to get vaccinated.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:19.000
- Definitely when I saw
that I had an opportunity

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.970
to get an appointment, and
I took the first available.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:23.680
There was no question in my mind.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:24.950
- [Narrator] He's even been volunteering

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:26.660
to help get people vaccinated,

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:29.210
and appeared in the school produced PSA.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:30.580
- If I could carry vaccines with me,

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:31.930
I'd just walk around
giving them to people.

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:32.763
It's that easy.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.790
- [Narrator] Like many
of the other schools

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:37.870
mandating the vaccine,
Northeastern says it will allow

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:40.530
for medical and religious exemptions.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:43.210
But Armini says that making
this announcement early

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:46.480
will allow vaccine hesitant
students to make other plans

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:49.210
because they won't be allowed on campus.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:50.800
- I mean, we hope it doesn't come to that.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.680
We hope that over the summer

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:56.510
anyone who may have
some vaccine hesitancy,

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:58.770
that that sort of dissipates over time.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:00.900
One thing that we always
find with students

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.060
is that peer to peer is very powerful.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:05.560
So if their friends are being vaccinated

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:08.230
and they're enthusiastic
about it, that helps a lot.

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:09.360
- [Narrator] Other colleges are hoping

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:12.120
they can reach herd
immunity without a mandate.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.020
Texas A&amp;M and Virginia Tech

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:16.700
believe the requirements
conflict with federal law

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:18.360
because the FDA has only allowed

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.730
the emergency use of the vaccines.

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:22.550
- I think a lot of it's just becoming

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:23.775
very politically charged,

00:03:23.775 --> 00:03:26.830
this debate around vaccine passports.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:29.940
By getting a vaccine you're
allowed to do certain things,

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:32.710
and by not getting it you're
left out of those things.

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:36.160
So places like Florida, Arizona, Texas,

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:39.700
Utah specifically says that
public higher ed institutions

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:43.810
are not allowed to require
vaccination of students,

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:47.060
faculty and staff in
order to be on campus.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.340
- [Narrator] The country's
largest university systems,

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:50.790
the University of California

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.680
and California State University,

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:55.200
recently announced they
intend to require vaccinations

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.810
for the more than a million
students and faculty,

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:00.090
but say the timing of
a more formal mandate

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:03.130
will depend on when the FDA
gives full authorization

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:05.070
to one or more of the vaccines.

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:07.653
It could come before
or after classes start.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:10.830
Many schools aren't wasting any time.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.470
They've launched vaccination blitzes

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:13.790
and public health campaigns

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:16.620
to get students immunized before
they leave for the summer.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:19.100
- Protecting the path, we're
all getting tested regularly,

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.850
making sure to fill out
our daily wellness checks.

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:23.800
- [Narrator] Last week Cornell University

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:26.630
in Ithaca, New York held
a pop-up vaccination event

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:29.540
on campus that provided
Moderna shots to students.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:31.300
The school says that nearly 50%

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:35.240
of the current on-campus
population is already vaccinated.

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:37.540
Senior Jade Ovadia says she's relieved

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:40.670
to see more and more of
her classmates vaccinated.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.890
- So I'm fully vaccinated,

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:45.090
as are many of the Cornell students.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.370
Everybody is very eager to get vaccinated.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:48.620
You know college life,

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:50.910
you only get to have it
really once in your life.

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:53.620
And COVID-19 kinda
interrupted that for us.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:55.790
And these are years that
we don't really get back.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:58.220
So I think we're all just
really eager and willing

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:00.990
to take whatever actions that will help us

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:03.163
be able to return back to that experience.

00:05:04.058 --> 00:05:06.244
(light upbeat music)

